# Platform scope

Read `PLATFORM.md`. This is one shared Next.js game (website + Capacitor iOS). Do not split repos or duplicate game screens unless the user explicitly asks for that.

The branch name `web-responsive` is not a website-only tree. It is the shared source for both platforms.

BEFORE any 1B Run change, classify the request internally as:

- WEBSITE ONLY
- IOS ONLY
- BOTH / SHARED

Rules:

- "website only" — do not change iOS behavior.
- "iOS only" — do not change website behavior.
- "both" — shared components may change.
- Do not assume a request applies to both platforms.
- A shared-file edit for a platform-specific feature must be guarded with `lib/platform/isNativeApp.ts`. Do not invent another platform check.
- Do not modify `ios/` unless native iOS/Capacitor behavior actually requires it.
- Do not create or run Supabase migrations unless the user specifically approves a backend/database change.
- Shared Supabase/backend changes affect the website and released iOS users.
- Keep one shared game. Editing shared code (`components/tradeup/`, `lib/`, `hooks/`, shared CSS) affects both platforms; iOS only receives it after `npm run build:ios` and a new Xcode build.
